"""fig3a_mse_reference_B.csv | main Fig. 3 (04_figures/fig.3/fig3_main_A4_v2.py)

Recovered statistical-analysis script | reproducibility package | Fig. 3 track.

WHAT THIS SCRIPT COMPUTES
    This code builds a per-model summary table of simulation accuracy from
    a per-subject MSE table. For each of nine models (spanning different
    simulation scales, data resolutions, and assimilation scales, plus SAR
    and rWW baselines), it pulls that model's column of per-subject MSE
    values, computes the mean and standard deviation (combined into a
    formatted "NP-edge MSE" string) and the median across the 12 subjects,
    and records which empirical FC reference was used for comparison. One
    row of the output table therefore represents a single model
    configuration, showing its labeled scale and resolution settings
    alongside the sample size, the empirical reference description, and
    the summary MSE statistics (mean-plus-std string and median)
    aggregated over the 12 subjects for that model.

INPUT FILES
    fig3a_mse_per_subject.csv

OUTPUT FILE
    fig3a_mse_reference_B.csv
    written to OUT_DIR (default /tmp/recovery_scratch/fig3)
    reference copy in this package: 04_figures/fig.3/fig3_data/fig3a_mse_reference_B.csv

STATISTICAL TESTS
    descriptive summary only (no inferential test in the recovered cell)

RUNNABLE ON A LAPTOP
    conditional on the input files above being present on this machine

SEED
    not applicable (deterministic computation)

PROVENANCE
    execution-log cell : 10783ea6-d4d3-4b01-812e-cd27be3faa14
    frame              : fe47a03f-2d43-4fe0-a1c3-e0544839d822
